The U.S. Navy will conduct naval operations on October 13, 15, and 16, 2026, daily between the hours of 1200 and 1630. Operations will be centered along the coastline near the following positions: 
32.849482, -118.368963; 
32.852276, -118.372688; 
32.855606, -118.377128; and 
32.858666, -118.381018. 

All mariners are advised to remain well clear of the operational area and maintain a safe clearance of at least 4 nautical miles offshore of the southeastern coastline of San Clemente Island. On-scene safety and escort vessels will actively monitor VHF-FM Channel 16. For live range status or coordination, contact FACSFAC San Diego or hail San Clemente Range Operations on VHF-FM Channel 16.
